[87.261308, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[KNow let me run it to confirm it works:\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;208m\u25b6 \u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;35m\u25cf \u001b[39m\u001b[2mRan bash(===============================================...) 0.1s\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[KDone. survey_report.py is created and verified \u2014 the real output is shown above.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1mWhat it does\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2022 Parses inline JSON (SURVEY_JSON) and prints a formatted terminal report with:\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u25e6 \u001b[1mHeader\u001b[22m: site, region, date, surveyors, area\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u25e6 \u001b[1mSummary\u001b[22m: species count, total individuals, density per hectare, average, most abundant\r\r\n\u001b[5G\u001b[K\u001b[1mBy type\u001b[22m: individuals grouped by taxon with percentage + ASCII bar chart\r\r\n\u001b[5G\u001b[K\u001b[1mConservation concern\u001b[22m: flagged species sorted by severity\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1mImportant note\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[KThe JSON from your message didn't arrive (your text cut off at the colon). I used a \u001b[1mrepresentative\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1msample dataset\u001b[22m so the script is fully runnable. To use your real data, just \u001b[1mreplace the SURVEY_JSON\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1mstring\u001b[22m. If your schema differs from what I assumed:\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K{\"survey\": {\"site\": ..., \"observations\": [{\"species\":..., \"type\":..., \"count\":..., \"status\":...}]}}\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[Kpa\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[2m \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;75m\u2191 54 above \u00b7 \u2193 1 below \u00b7 Shift+\u2191\u2193 \u00b7 End \u2913\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[2m \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;